# Git "Push" Workflow

When the user says **push** (without further qualification), execute this workflow on **main**:

1. **Commit** all changes on `main` (stage everything relevant, write a commit message, commit)
2. **Push** `main` to `origin`

"Saying push" is explicit permission to commit — treat it as a commit request.

For any other variation (e.g. "just commit", "push without committing"), follow the user's exact wording.

## Examples

| User says | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| "push" | commit main → push main |
| "just commit" | commit only (no push) |
